# AmigaOne X5000: Kconfig entry for the x86 BIOS emulator, which upstream
# v2021.04 builds (drivers/Makefile) but offers no symbol for.
#

config BIOSEMU
	bool "Enable the x86 BIOS emulator (run a video card's VBIOS)"
	help
	  Enable the SciTech x86 real-mode BIOS emulator (drivers/bios_emulator).
	  It POSTs a PCI/PCIe VGA card's x86 Video BIOS on a non-x86 host so the
	  card sets up a (VESA) framebuffer. Required on PowerPC boards such as the
	  AmigaOne X5000 (Varisys Cyrus) that drive a Radeon card through its own
	  VBIOS rather than a native U-Boot video driver.

	  Boards using this must also define VIDEO_IO_OFFSET (the base added to
	  emulated x86 I/O ports so they reach the card's PCIe I/O window) and, to
	  actually set a linear mode, CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_SET_VESA_MODE.
